  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Reduce TB</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Democratic Republic of the Congo):  .USAID Reduce Tuberculosis (TB) is one of two USAID activities in the DRC that is a part of the Local Organizations Network. In support of USAID&apos;s Global Accelerator to End Tuberculosis, this activity facilitates and sustains new partnerships, fosters inclusiveness, and promotes advocacy, empowerment, and accountability for improved TB service delivery in the DRC..USAID Reduce TB will use FY 2022 funds to equip local communities and health service providers in three provinces (Haut-Katanga, Haut-Lomami, and Lualaba) to better manage and deliver TB prevention, treatment, and care interventions. The activity will collaborate with the Ministry of Health and provincial TB coordination structures to identify TB cases and support TB patients and their households to successfully complete treatment and initiate preventive therapy. Partnerships with local organizations, including civil society organizations, faith-based organizations, private sector service delivery providers, and academic institutions, will drive the implementation of locally developed solutions to improve TB diagnosis, treatment, and prevention services, which advances USAID&apos;s Localization Agenda...This activity will contribute to Mission Objective 4.1 (Strengthen institutional and community capacity to prevent outbreaks from becoming pandemics as well as respond to and overcome frequent public health and humanitarian emergencies) by increasing country capacity, ownership, and accountability towards a more sustainable and effective TB program for the Congolese population. This activity strengthens DRC&apos;s capacity to prevent, detect, and respond to infectious diseases, thereby benefiting U.S. national security interests....</narrative>
  </description>
